  "caption": "Quinn joined two cricket teams, threw everything in preseason, and by week three the shoulder said no thanks.\n\nThrowing shoulders often get sore when load outpaces what the shoulder can handle, rather than from one weak muscle. Sudden preseason spikes and playing for several teams are common setups.\n\nWhat may help: track throws and plan rest days, strengthen the rotator cuff and shoulder blade, let the legs and trunk share the work, keep the mid-back mobile, and return after a break in stages.\n\nGet it checked if you notice lost speed or accuracy, a dead arm feeling, or soreness lasting beyond a day or two. Young throwers with elbow pain should stop throwing and get assessed.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
